             :intent "One `my.test/run-owned` of seon.error.refusal-test (17 tests, 9.9 s, 1.07M armed calls) on a branch agent settled 1,718 datoms in its evaluation's transaction, 1,566 of them :seon.profile.measurement upserts (294 rows: at 294, calls 294, p99 286, p50 208, errors 133, plus 117 new ids with sym/digest/id), out of 2,139 datoms and 253 files / 843 KB for the whole run (default pid 30874, 2026-10-07, db-watch lane). significant-tx writes a row for every executed definition whose quantile bucket moved, and measurements are branch data, so every agent branch re-measures the same platform functions from scratch and none of it merges. The only reader is seon.health's digest comparison (latest p50 per [sym digest]). Smallest fix at the producer: write a measurement only for definitions the evaluation changed (their digest is new) or on the cluster branch, never per agent branch, and without :at/:calls churn when the bucket did not move. Done when a repeated run-owned of the same namespace on a branch writes under 50 measurement datoms, measured with watch.clj :since-basis, with a regression on the count."
